## 3. Project 1: Full Audit — LiquidityForecasting

### 3.1 What it does

P1 estimates daily net cash moving through currency accounts, projects future balances, identifies minimum-buffer breaches, and distributes a limited central funding pool. Its intended users are treasury analysts managing several currencies. The distinction between cashflow and balance matters: a negative daily flow is not necessarily a liquidity shortfall if the account has enough opening cash.

The user selects sample data or uploads dated net-cashflow columns, selects currencies and a 7–90-day horizon, sets opening balances/buffers/FX/costs/priorities, and receives forecasts, shortfalls and funding recommendations. The default CLI forecasts 30 days. The dashboard backtest is fixed at three seven-day folds even when the displayed forecast horizon is longer. [P1-app], lines 71–279, 335–390; [P1-main], lines 29–95.

