### 3.5 Reliability, strengths, limitations and prioritized improvements

**Strongest demonstrated capabilities:** reproducible synthetic data; chronological baseline evaluation; tested balance/buffer arithmetic; tested FX conversion; tested constrained funding allocation. These are useful foundations. The architecture separates data, forecasting, evaluation, balances, FX and allocation, making replacement and diagnosis practical. The README candidly identifies synthetic data and maximum-shortfall limitations. [P1-data]; [P1-evaluation]; [P1-readme], 197–216.

**Best verified forecasting evidence:** the seasonal-naive baseline, with all 18 folds in Section 7. There is no verified SARIMAX result and no documented numerical SARIMAX benchmark to select as “best.” Comparing raw EUR and JPY MAE would be meaningless.

**Technical and product gaps:** missing dependencies prevent full reproduction; no environment lock; no interval calibration; no per-horizon evaluation of 30/90 days; no nonfinite/gap validation; no persistent forecasts, authentication, audit trail or scheduled ingestion. The dashboard has useful risk warnings and editable assumptions, but the Excel interval omission and all-history chart with mixed currency scales weaken reporting. [P1-app], 111–112, 335–390, 473–492.

**Funding caveat:** the LP includes fees in its objective but not its cash budget. If the same central account pays transfer fees, budget conservation is incomplete. Priority is a user weight, not a calibrated probability or monetary loss. The LP can rationally leave cash unused when cost exceeds priority, so full funding is not an unconditional property. [P1-allocation], 149–156.

| Priority | Improvement | Impact | Effort |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Package a reproducible environment and run SARIMAX-versus-naive rolling evaluation with per-fold model identity and saved predictions | Establishes whether the learned model adds value | Medium |
| 2 | Reject nonfinite values and invalid frequency; define missing-flow semantics and test timestamp alignment | Prevents silent accounting/evaluation errors | Low–medium |
| 3 | Evaluate long horizons, balance-path risk and calibrated intervals using training-only residuals | Makes liquidity risk outputs meaningful | Medium–high |
| 4 | Add dated funding constraints, fee cash accounting and operational transfer timing | Makes recommendations operationally coherent | High |
| 5 | Pass interval results into dashboard export and version data/assumptions/results | Fixes report completeness and traceability | Low–medium |

Readiness: **analytical demonstration with tested components**, not a verified production treasury system.

