### 5.5 Reliability and concrete inconsistencies

1. **Future-target contamination is explicit:** act is copied from generated future rows; model curves are functions of act. This is not merely a possible leakage risk. It prevents interpreting the dashboard error as out-of-sample predictive quality. [P3-html], 765–768.
2. **Documentation proposes test-set tuning:** README line 200 says SLSQP minimizes MAE on the test set. Even if the missing trainer follows that description, that set would become a model-selection set and require a separate untouched holdout. This is a documented methodological risk, not a verified missing-code behavior. General methodological support: [scikit-learn leakage guidance](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/common_pitfalls).
3. **Data sizes disagree:** README/UI claim 2,557 days; uploaded CSV has 1,096 daily rows; browser has 730 historical plus 90 future rows. The CSV is never loaded by the page. [P3-readme], 62; [P3-html], 691, 742, 1231; A10–A11.
4. **Accounting does not reconcile on weekends:** generator keeps positive outflow while forcing net=0 and leaving cumulative cash unchanged. Audit found 235 such weekend rows among 820 total. Another 148 net-versus-rounded-inflow-minus-rounded-outflow differences are rounding effects; these should not be confused with the substantive weekend defect. [P3-html], 755–761.
5. **Scenarios do not implement the stated economic shock:** inflow is scaled while outflow stays unchanged in some charts, but net and cumulative cash are simply multiplied elsewhere. For a pure inflow shock, net should be scaled_inflow−unchanged_outflow. Existing logic also scales historical cumulative balances. [P3-html], 826–840, 880–904.
6. **Interval claims conflict:** UI reports 93.8% coverage; PDF says “PI Coverage 95%”; actual generated 90-point interval containment is 100%. None establishes calibration. For negative predictions, .82×value exceeds 1.18×value, reversing lower/upper order. [P3-html], 592, 769, 1433.
7. **Charts/report names mislead:** “30-Day Rolling Forecast” is the first 30 static future rows; “Monthly ... last 12M” aggregates all 730 historical days by month; “Min Liquidity 30D” is historical, not a future risk floor. [P3-html], 622, 834, 882, 901–904, 999–1014.
8. **Financial signs and time labels:** currency formatter fI and PDF sfI use absolute values, potentially hiding deficits. PDF dated 27 March 2026 displays forecast dates starting 31 December with no year; code's actual forecast interval is 31 December 2024–30 March 2025. [P3-html], 772, 1242–1251, 1558–1567; [P3-pdf], pages 1/4.
9. **Metric explanation errors:** README says RMSE lower than MAE means no outliers; for the same residual set RMSE≥MAE. R² can be negative, so it is not bounded to 0–1. The “real data 4–8% MAPE” range is an unsupported expectation. [P3-readme], 247–254.
10. **No actual feature attribution or training curve:** the 15 feature weights are literals; “Huber loss” is a generated decay. The UI's SHAP/AdamW labels have no corresponding computation. [P3-html], 660–665, 1116–1117, 1146–1147.

