### 7.3 Metric interpretation, fixtures and other claimed scores

P1's original backtest computes fold-level MAE and MASE only; no RMSE, R², MAPE, sMAPE, lead-specific error or interval coverage is persisted. The six aggregate rows above average three equal-size folds. MASE uses each fold's **training** seven-day absolute-difference mean; average fold MASE is not pooled MAE divided by one global scale. MASE<1 compares against the training-scale benchmark, not automatically against the held-out naive forecast. [P1-evaluation], 58–83, 174–179.

